<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 265)</h2>
<p><b>Web Review grows up</b> — real transport, and the browser can drive.</p>
<ul>
<li>The web page now has a proper transport bar, a timeline with comment markers, timecode and frame readouts, keyboard control — and it looks like Asobi, not a prototype.</li>
<li><b>Web clients can drive the session</b>: their scrubs and play/pause move every seat, exactly like a native guest. Follow-the-host now honors stop — when you park on a frame, so do they.</li>
<li><b>Late joiners get the whole conversation</b>: existing comments and markup now arrive on join — in the app too, which quietly had the same gap.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
